  "packageSize": 50014120,
  "projectUrl": "https://www.questpdf.com/",
  "published": "2026-11-12T16:36:24.59Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Updated Skia to m158.\n- Fixed a rare issue where a Table with row spans could generate empty pages endlessly.\n- Changed the default value of Settings.EnableDetailedLayoutErrors to false, so layout errors are reported immediately. Finding the root cause of a layout error can be time-consuming and resource-intensive. Enable this setting during development to get detailed diagnostics.\n- Soft hyphens and zero-width spaces no longer appear as spaces in the PDF text layer, which improves screen reader output, text search, and copy-paste.\n- Increased the maximum number of font families in a fallback chain from 16 to 128.\n- Increased the maximum number of font features per text style from 16 to 32.\n- Improved the stability of the Column element. Spacing is now applied only between items that have height, so hidden items no longer leave empty gaps.\n- Fixed rare cases where PreventPageBreak and EnsureSpace could cause a layout exception or endless document generation.\n- Fixed SVG rendering of dashed lines, where an additional hairline was drawn between the dashes.\n- When the default port is occupied, ShowInCompanion now connects to the Companion App on the nearest available port.\n- Improved the reliability of launching and connecting to the Companion App (requires updating the Companion App to the newest version).\n- When a document is too complex for a responsive preview in the Companion App, the library now throws an exception that explains the problem.\n- Renamed the native files shipped with the library to follow the snake_case convention (for example, questpdf_skia and questpdf_qpdf). Deployment scripts that reference these files by name must be updated.",
